        },
        "texto": "We find the practice of writing on rods alluded to as early as the time of Moses. See Numbers 17:2. A similar practice was known among the Greeks. The laws of Solon, which were preserved at Athens, were written on billets of wood called axones. These were of a square or pyramidal…"
